The Owner and collaborators or agents acting within the Owner's express
project-specific authorization may perform the work that authorization permits.
Repository access or contributor status alone is not such authorization, and
work for the Owner grants no independent reuse rights to a collaborator.

## 4. No general implementation-reuse permission

Except for a separate written grant signed by the Owner, the limited operating
permission in section 2, or rights preserved by section 7, no permission is
granted to copy, extract, modify, adapt, translate, distribute, sublicense, sell,
rehost, self-host, or incorporate the Materials or their protected portions in
another project, service, package, template, dataset, or product. Attribution
does not substitute for permission. Small or general-purpose functions are not
exceptions merely because they are reusable.

There is no automatic exception for personal, noncommercial, educational,
nonprofit, research, governmental, or other institutional use. The same
Official Product entitlement rules apply to those users. A commercial customer
may use an Official Product at work within the purchased scope without thereby
receiving permission to reuse or redistribute its implementation.

No grant is made to extract the protected Materials for machine-learning model training,
fine-tuning, retrieval, prompting, evaluation, or derived implementations. This
does not prohibit the Owner's authorized agents, documented Official Product
functionality, independently created material, or uses allowed without the
Owner's permission under applicable law. No contractual restriction here
overrides a non-waivable right to reverse engineer, interoperate, repair, make
an accessibility adaptation, or conduct otherwise lawful analysis.

